use std
into human_cad.amni
dialect js

This file is a WebAssembly library built with `--web` for Amni-CAD; its `main()` does nothing and every function starting with `hc_` is exported to `cad/he/host.js`. It implements the parametric anatomical quad-mesh human generator, ANSUR II anthropometric proportion solver, 25 body and 25 facial morphs, 52 ARKit FACS expression blendshapes, 71-bone humanoid rig with twist bones, 30 finger phalanges and facial bones, volume-preserving dual-blend joint posing, body-fitted shell garment generator with anti-poke-through clamping, general-purpose mesh shrinkwrap and proportional falloff editing, 31 semantic anatomical vertex/face regions, 39 3D landmarks, and quantitative character diagnostics. Coordinates follow Amni-CAD: Z is up (soles at Z equal to 0, crown at Z equal to stature), negative Y is forward, positive X is the character's left, and negative X is the character's right. Reals are f64 in parameter/rig/audit buffers and f32 in mesh attribute buffers.

```amni
extern fn hc_view_f64(id i32, xs real[:]) = "hc_view_f64";
extern fn hc_view_f32(id i32, xs f32[:]) = "hc_view_f32";
extern fn hc_view_i32(id i32, xs i32[:]) = "hc_view_i32";
extern fn hc_view_u8(id i32, xs u8[:]) = "hc_view_u8";
let PI real = 3.141592653589793;
let D2R real = 0.017453292519943295;
let ST_Z real[24] = [0.472,0.512,0.552,0.595,0.648,0.698,0.742,0.785,0.818,0.838,0.858,0.875,0.885,0.897,0.904,0.911,0.920,0.930,0.941,0.948,0.955,0.970,0.984,0.997];
let ST_RX real[24] = [0.088,0.102,0.098,0.082,0.089,0.098,0.105,0.112,0.108,0.048,0.035,0.039,0.045,0.048,0.050,0.052,0.054,0.055,0.055,0.055,0.054,0.053,0.050,0.032];
let ST_RYF real[24] = [0.058,0.070,0.064,0.055,0.062,0.074,0.078,0.070,0.055,0.038,0.035,0.052,0.062,0.064,0.063,0.065,0.064,0.072,0.062,0.059,0.061,0.064,0.059,0.038];
let ST_RYB real[24] = [0.070,0.084,0.072,0.058,0.065,0.072,0.075,0.070,0.058,0.042,0.038,0.044,0.048,0.052,0.055,0.058,0.061,0.063,0.065,0.067,0.065,0.063,0.058,0.038];
let ST_REG i32[24] = [1,1,1,2,3,3,3,4,4,5,5,7,7,8,8,8,9,9,10,10,10,11,12,12];
let LEG_T real[11] = [0.0,0.13,0.28,0.44,0.48,0.52,0.68,0.84,0.92,0.97,1.0];
let LEG_R real[11] = [0.058,0.055,0.049,0.040,0.038,0.037,0.041,0.029,0.025,0.028,0.024];
let ARM_T real[10] = [0.0,0.12,0.28,0.45,0.50,0.55,0.75,0.92,0.97,1.0];
let ARM_R real[10] = [0.040,0.035,0.031,0.027,0.025,0.025,0.023,0.018,0.022,0.024];
let FNG_L real[5] = [0.034,0.048,0.053,0.049,0.039];
let FNG_R real[5] = [0.0072,0.0064,0.0067,0.0062,0.0054];
let BPAR_TAB i32[71] = [-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,5,5,5,5,5,5,3,3,3,15,16,16,18,18,20,21,22,21,24,25,21,27,28,21,30,31,21,33,34,3,36,37,37,39,39,41,42,43,42,45,46,42,48,49,42,51,52,42,54,55,0,57,57,59,59,61,61,0,64,64,66,66,68,68];
```

Module state. Ints starting at 0: `NV`, `NQ`, `NT`, `GNV`, `GNQ`, `GNT`, `SNV`, `SNT`, `WITH_EYES`. Growable arrays: f64 `MP` (50 morph parameters), `FC` (52 FACS weights), `BP` (213 bone Euler degrees, 3 per bone for 71 bones), `BH` (213 bone head coordinates), `BT` (213 bone tail coordinates), `LM` (117 landmark coordinates, 3 per landmark for 39 landmarks), `AUD` (25 diagnostic metrics), `WM` (852 world bone matrix entries, 12 per bone: 9 rotation plus 3 translation), `BM` (852 bind bone matrix entries); f32 `POS`, `REST`, `NRM`, `UV`, `WW`, `GPOS`, `GNRM`, `GUV`, `GWW`, `SPOS`, `SNRM`, `TPOS`, `XF`; i32 `BPAR`, `QUAD`, `TRI`, `JW`, `GQUAD`, `GTRI`, `GJW`, `STRI`, `VROW`, `XI`; u8 `VREG`, `FREG`, `SMASK`, `ZU`.

Sizing and push helpers. `zf(xs, n int)` takes an f64 growable array by reference: xs is emptied, then gets `reserve`(n), then is resized to n entries of 0.0. `zf32(xs, n int)` does the same for an f32 growable array with 0.0 as f32. `zi(xs, n int, v int)` does the same for an i32 growable array with v as i32. `zu(xs, n int)` does the same for a u8 growable array with 0. `cwf(xs, m int)` takes an f32 growable array by reference and ensures xs.cap is at least m using `XF` as scratch: when m is above xs.cap, `XF` is emptied, then gets `reserve`(the length of xs), then gets xs via `append`, xs is emptied, then gets `reserve`(m), then gets `XF` via `append`, and `XF` is emptied. `cwi(xs, m int)` does the same for an i32 growable array using `XI` as scratch. `cwu(xs, m int)` does the same for a u8 growable array using `ZU` as scratch. `puf(xs, v real)` grows xs with cwf to twice its length plus 128 when full, then pushes v as f32. `pui(xs, v int)` grows xs with cwi to twice its length plus 128 when full, then pushes v as i32. `puu(xs, v int)` grows xs with cwu to twice its length plus 128 when full, then pushes v as u8.

Math helpers. `cl(x real, a real, b real) real` returns a when x is below a, b when x is above b, and x otherwise. `lrp(a real, b real, t real) real` returns a plus (b minus a) times t. `smstep(a real, b real, x real) real`: t is cl((x minus a) divided by (b minus a), 0.0, 1.0); it returns (t times t) times (3.0 minus 2.0 times t). `gauss(x real, c real, w real) real`: d is (x minus c) divided by w; it returns math::exp(the negation of (d times d)). `len3(x real, y real, z real) real` returns sqrt((x times x plus y times y) plus z times z).

Vertex and quad emission helpers. `addv(x real, y real, z real, u real, v real, reg int, b0 int, w0 real, b1 int, w1 real, b2 int, w2 real, b3 int, w3 real) int` appends one vertex to the mesh and returns its index (which is `NV` before incrementing `NV` by 1): it pushes x, y, z onto `REST` and `POS` with puf, pushes 0.0 three times onto `NRM` with puf, pushes u and v onto `UV` with puf, pushes reg onto `VREG` with puu, normalizes the four non-negative weights (when their sum s is above 1e-9 each weight is divided by s, otherwise w0 becomes 1.0 and the other three 0.0), pushes b0, b1, b2, b3 onto `JW` with pui, and pushes the four normalized weights onto `WW` with puf. `addq(a int, b int, c int, d int, reg int)` appends one quad (a, b, c, d) to `QUAD` with pui, appends reg to `FREG` with puu, increments `NQ` by 1, and appends the two triangles (a, b, c) and (a, c, d) to `TRI` with pui while incrementing `NT` by 2.

Normals helper `recalc_nrm(ps, tr, nt int, nr, nv int)` takes const f32 slice ps, const i32 slice tr, triangle count nt, f32 growable array nr by reference, and vertex count nv: nr is resized with zf32(nr, 3 times nv). For t from 0 below nt: a, b, c are tr[3 times t] as int, tr[3 times t plus 1] as int, tr[3 times t plus 2] as int; ax, ay, az are ps[3 times a] as real, ps[3 times a plus 1] as real, ps[3 times a plus 2] as real; e1x, e1y, e1z are (ps[3 times b] as real) minus ax, (ps[3 times b plus 1] as real) minus ay, (ps[3 times b plus 2] as real) minus az; e2x, e2y, e2z are (ps[3 times c] as real) minus ax, (ps[3 times c plus 1] as real) minus ay, (ps[3 times c plus 2] as real) minus az; nx is e1y times e2z minus e1z times e2y, ny is e1z times e2x minus e1x times e2z, nz is e1x times e2y minus e1y times e2x; for each corner v among a, b and c, nr[3 times v] grows by nx as f32, nr[3 times v plus 1] grows by ny as f32, and nr[3 times v plus 2] grows by nz as f32. Then for v from 0 below nv: lx, ly, lz are nr[3 times v] as real, nr[3 times v plus 1] as real, nr[3 times v plus 2] as real; L is len3(lx, ly, lz); when L is above 1e-12, nr[3 times v] becomes (lx divided by L) as f32, nr[3 times v plus 1] becomes (ly divided by L) as f32, and nr[3 times v plus 2] becomes (lz divided by L) as f32; otherwise nr[3 times v plus 2] becomes 1.0 as f32.

`refresh_views()` reports all module views to JavaScript: hc_view_f64(1, `MP`), hc_view_f64(2, `FC`), hc_view_f64(3, `BP`), hc_view_f64(4, `BH`), hc_view_f64(5, `BT`), hc_view_i32(7, `BPAR`), hc_view_f64(8, `LM`), hc_view_f64(9, `AUD`), hc_view_f32(10, `POS`), hc_view_f32(11, `REST`), hc_view_f32(12, `NRM`), hc_view_f32(13, `UV`), hc_view_i32(14, `QUAD`), hc_view_i32(15, `TRI`), hc_view_u8(17, `VREG`), hc_view_u8(18, `FREG`), hc_view_i32(19, `JW`), hc_view_f32(20, `WW`), hc_view_f32(21, `GPOS`), hc_view_f32(22, `GNRM`), hc_view_f32(23, `GUV`), hc_view_i32(24, `GQUAD`), hc_view_i32(25, `GTRI`), hc_view_i32(27, `GJW`), hc_view_f32(28, `GWW`), hc_view_f32(29, `SPOS`), hc_view_i32(30, `STRI`), hc_view_f32(31, `TPOS`), hc_view_u8(32, `SMASK`).

`hc_defaults()` is exported. It initializes `MP` (50 reals), `FC` (52 reals), `BP` (213 reals), `BH` (213 reals), `BT` (213 reals), `BPAR` (71 i32s copied from `BPAR_TAB`), `LM` (117 reals), `AUD` (25 reals), `WM` (852 reals), and `BM` (852 reals). Default `MP` values: `MP`[0] (sex, 0 female to 1 male) becomes 0.5; `MP`[1] (age in years) becomes 28.0; `MP`[2] (stature in meters) becomes 1.75; `MP`[3] (muscle) becomes 0.5; `MP`[4] (weight) becomes 0.5; `MP`[5] (proportions) becomes 0.75; `MP`[7] (shoulder_breadth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[8] (chest_depth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[9] (bust_cup) becomes 0.35; `MP`[10] (waist_breadth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[11] (hip_breadth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[12] (arm_length) becomes 1.0; `MP`[13] (leg_length) becomes 1.0; `MP`[14] (thigh_girth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[15] (calf_girth) becomes 1.0; `MP`[17] (head_scale) becomes 1.0; `MP`[18] (arm_down_deg, A-pose angle below horizontal) becomes 35.0; `MP`[19] (stance_width) becomes 1.0; `MP`[20] (glute_volume) becomes 0.5; `MP`[21] (neck_thick) becomes 1.0; facial sliders `MP`[25] through `MP`[49] start at 0.0 (25 jaw_width, 27 jaw_angle, 28 chin_height, 29 chin_prominence, 30 cheek_bones, 31 cheek_fullness, 32 nose_length, 33 nose_width, 34 nose_bridge, 35 nose_tip_up, 37 lip_upper, 38 lip_lower, 39 mouth_width, 40 eye_size, 41 eye_spacing, 42 eye_tilt, 43 brow_height, 44 brow_ridge, 45 forehead_slope, 47 ear_size, 48 ear_out, 49 cranium_width). It calls refresh_views().

`hc_info(wh i32) i32` is exported and returns mesh counts: `NV` as i32 when wh equals 0, `NQ` as i32 when wh equals 1, `NT` as i32 when wh equals 2, `GNV` as i32 when wh equals 3, `GNQ` as i32 when wh equals 4, `GNT` as i32 when wh equals 5, 71 when wh equals 7, and 39 when wh equals 8.

Finger extrusion helper `extrude_finger(q0 int, q1 int, q2 int, q3 int, len real, rad real, side int, fi int, b_base int, reg int, curl real)`: takes four palm quad corner vertex indices (q0, q1, q2, q3) whose outward normal points along the digit direction, insets them by 0.18 toward their centroid (cx, cy, cz) with averaged UV (cu, cv) to form four web-collar vertices u0, u1, u2, u3 weighted 0.55 to the hand bone (21 when side is above 0, else 42) and 0.45 to b_base, emits the four web-collar quads (q0, q1, u1, u0), (q1, q2, u2, u1), (q2, q3, u3, u2) and (q3, q0, u0, u3) with region reg minus 1, and records `BH` of b_base at (cx, cy, cz). Compute the quad diagonal outward normal (dx, dy, dz) as the normalized cross product of (`REST`[q2] minus `REST`[q0]) with (`REST`[q3] minus `REST`[q1]) so a mirrored quad `(q3', q2', q1', q0')` produces the exact X-mirrored normal `(-dx, dy, dz)`. For phalanx step p from 0 below 3: t is (p plus 1) as real divided by 3.0; taper is 1.0 minus 0.28 times t; step_len is len times (0.42 when p equals 0, 0.33 when p equals 1, and 0.25 otherwise); bend is curl times (p plus 1) as real times D2R; dir_x is dx times math::cos(bend), dir_y is dy, dir_z is dz times math::cos(bend) minus math::sin(bend) times 0.5; dl is len3(dir_x, dir_y, dir_z); ux, uy, uz are dir_x divided by dl, dir_y divided by dl, dir_z divided by dl; the ring center advances by step_len along (ux, uy, uz); bone_cur is b_base plus (1 when fi equals 0 and p is above 1, else p); `BT` of bone_cur becomes the new ring center, and when p is below 2 and (fi is not 0 or p equals 0) `BH` of (bone_cur plus 1) becomes the new ring center; four new vertices w0, w1, w2, w3 are placed around the new ring center by scaling each corner's offset from the previous center by taper (clamped to radius rad times taper), weighted 0.8 to bone_cur and 0.2 to (bone_cur minus 1 when p is above 0, else hand bone), with region reg; four quads (u0, u1, w1, w0), (u1, u2, w2, w1), (u2, u3, w3, w2) and (u3, u0, w0, w3) are emitted with region reg; u0, u1, u2, u3 become w0, w1, w2, w3. Finally one fingertip cap quad (u0, u1, u2, u3) is emitted with region reg.

`hc_build(with_eyes i32) i32` is exported and generates the complete parametric watertight quad-loop human mesh, 71-bone skeleton, 39 landmarks, normals, FACS offsets, pose and audit, returning `NV` as i32. First `NV`, `NQ`, `NT` become 0, `WITH_EYES` becomes with_eyes as int, and `POS`, `REST`, `NRM`, `UV`, `QUAD`, `TRI`, `VREG`, `FREG`, `JW`, `WW` are emptied and reserved (`REST`, `POS`, `NRM` to 12000; `UV` to 8000; `QUAD`, `JW`, `WW` to 15000; `TRI` to 24000; `VREG`, `FREG` to 4000), while `VROW` is sized with zi(`VROW`, 480, -1). Read macros: sex is cl(`MP`[0], 0.0, 1.0); H is cl(`MP`[2], 0.5, 2.8); mus is cl(`MP`[3], 0.0, 1.0); wt is cl(`MP`[4], 0.0, 1.0); prop is cl(`MP`[5], 0.0, 1.0); sh_k is cl(`MP`[7], 0.7, 1.4) times lrp(0.93, 1.09, sex) times (1.0 plus 0.08 times (mus minus 0.5)); ch_k is cl(`MP`[8], 0.75, 1.35) times (1.0 plus 0.12 times (wt minus 0.5) plus 0.07 times (mus minus 0.5)); cup is cl(`MP`[9], 0.0, 1.0) times (1.0 minus 0.82 times sex); wa_k is cl(`MP`[10], 0.7, 1.5) times lrp(0.89, 1.04, sex) times (1.0 plus 0.28 times (wt minus 0.5) minus 0.07 times (mus minus 0.5)); hp_k is cl(`MP`[11], 0.75, 1.4) times lrp(1.05, 0.94, sex) times (1.0 plus 0.18 times (wt minus 0.5)); leg_k is cl(`MP`[13], 0.82, 1.18) times lrp(0.98, 1.03, prop); arm_k is cl(`MP`[12], 0.82, 1.18); hd_k is cl(`MP`[17], 0.8, 1.25) times lrp(1.04, 0.98, prop); nk_k is cl(`MP`[21], 0.75, 1.35) times lrp(0.92, 1.10, sex); glute_k is cl(`MP`[20], 0.0, 1.0); stance_k is cl(`MP`[19], 0.5, 1.5); arm_deg is cl(`MP`[18], 0.0, 75.0).

Torso, neck and head rings (`s` from 0 below 24, `k` from 0 below 20). Skip creating the 4 unused interior vertices of the two 2-by-3 shoulder openings (`s` equal to 7 with `k` equal to 4, 5, 14 or 15, leaving `VROW`[20 times s plus k] equal to -1 so zero loose vertices exist). For each station s from 0 below 24: zf0 is `ST_Z`[s]; zf is zf0 times leg_k when zf0 is at most 0.52, lrp(0.52 times leg_k, 0.875, (zf0 minus 0.52) divided by 0.355) when zf0 is at most 0.875, and 0.875 plus (zf0 minus 0.875) times hd_k otherwise; z is zf times H. Scale factors on rx, ryf (front, negative Y) and ryb (back, positive Y): for hip stations (s at most 2) sx is hp_k, syf is ch_k, syb is hp_k times (1.0 plus 0.22 times (glute_k minus 0.5)); for waist (s equals 3 or 4) sx is wa_k, syf is wa_k times (1.0 plus 0.25 times cl(wt minus 0.4, 0.0, 1.0)), syb is ch_k; for chest and shoulder (s from 5 through 8) sx is lrp(wa_k, sh_k, (s minus 4) as real divided by 4.0), syf is ch_k, syb is ch_k; for neck (s equals 9 or 10) sx is nk_k, syf is nk_k, syb is nk_k; for head (s at least 11) sx is hd_k times (1.0 plus 0.12 times `MP`[49]), syf is hd_k, syb is hd_k. Spine S-curve offset y_sp in Y: 0.012 times H times math::sin(((zf0 minus 0.47) divided by 0.40) times 2.0 times PI) when s is below 11, and negative 0.008 times H when s is at least 11. Bone weights for station s: pelvis (0) and spine_01 (1) for s at most 2, spine_01 (1) and spine_02 (2) for s equals 3 or 4, spine_02 (2) and spine_03 (3) for s from 5 through 8, neck_01 (4) and head (5) for s equals 9 or 10, jaw (6) blended with head (5) on chin and lower-lip front for s from 11 through 14, and head (5) for s at least 11. For each non-skipped k from 0 below 20: th is (2.0 times PI) times ((k as real plus 0.5) divided by 20.0); sn is math::sin(th); cs is math::cos(th); x0 is (`ST_RX`[s] times sx times H) times sn; ry is (`ST_RYF`[s] times syf) when cs is at least 0.0 else (`ST_RYB`[s] times syb); y0 is y_sp minus (ry times H) times cs; z0 is z. Apply bilaterally symmetric anatomical sculpting on (x0, y0, z0) so k and 19 minus k have exact (-x0, y0, z0) mirror coordinates: on chest stations s equals 5 or 6 when cs is above 0.25, add bilateral breast/pectoral prominence along negative Y proportional to (cup times 0.038 plus mus times 0.012) times H times gauss(math::fabs(sn), 0.52, 0.28), weighted 0.35 to breast_l (13) when sn is above 0 else breast_r (14); on glute stations s equals 0 or 1 when cs is below negative 0.2, push positive Y by (0.018 plus 0.022 times glute_k) times H times gauss(math::fabs(sn), 0.45, 0.32) and add subtle gluteal cleft at small |sn|; on back stations s from 2 through 7 when cs is below negative 0.85, indent spinal groove slightly by negative 0.005 times H; on head stations s at least 11, apply facial anatomy and the 25 facial sliders symmetrically in |sn|: jaw width (`MP`[25]) and jaw angle (`MP`[27]) widen x0 on s from 11 through 14; chin height (`MP`[28]) and chin prominence (`MP`[29]) shift z0 and negative Y at s equals 11 and 12 near front (cs above 0.7); lower lip (s equals 13) and upper lip (s equals 15) push negative Y by (0.008 plus 0.009 times `MP`[38] or `MP`[37]) times H times hd_k when cs is above 0.82, while mouth rima (s equals 14) indents positive Y by 0.004 times H and mouth width (`MP`[39]) scales front X; nose bridge (s equals 18) and nose tip (s equals 16 and 17) project negative Y at front (cs above 0.90) by (0.019 plus 0.010 times `MP`[32] or `MP`[34]) times H times hd_k, nose tip Z shifts by 0.005 times `MP`[35] times H, and alar nose width (`MP`[33]) widens s equals 16; orbital sockets (s from 18 through 20, |sn| near 0.34 plus 0.05 times `MP`[41], cs above 0.55) recess positive Y by (0.010 plus 0.004 times `MP`[40]) times H times hd_k and shift Z symmetrically by 0.02 times kH times `MP`[42] times (math::fabs(sn) minus 0.34); cheekbones (`MP`[30]) and cheek fullness (`MP`[31]) project s equals 17 and 18 around |sn| equal to 0.58; brow ridge (s equals 21, cs above 0.65) projects negative Y by (0.007 plus 0.008 times `MP`[44] plus 0.004 times sex) times H and shifts Z by 0.005 times `MP`[43] times H; forehead slope (`MP`[45]) shifts s equals 22 Y; ears (s from 16 through 19, |sn| above 0.94) project outward in X by sign(sn) times (0.011 plus 0.007 times `MP`[47] plus 0.005 times `MP`[48]) times H times hd_k. Vertex region reg is refined from `ST_REG`[s] (chin/jaw 7, lips 8, nose 9 when cs is above 0.88 on s 16 through 18, eyes 10 when cs is above 0.55 on s 18 through 20, brow 11 on s 21 front, ears 13 when |sn| is above 0.93 on s 16 through 19, cheek 14 on s 16 through 18 mid-front, cranium 12 otherwise on head). Store the returned `addv` vertex index in `VROW`[20 times s plus k].

Torso quad connectivity and crown cap. Emit torso quads `addq`(`VROW`[20 times s plus k], `VROW`[20 times s plus ((k plus 1) mod 20)], `VROW`[20 times (s plus 1) plus ((k plus 1) mod 20)], `VROW`[20 times (s plus 1) plus k], reg) for every s from 0 below 23 and k from 0 below 20 EXCEPT the two X-mirrored 2-by-3 shoulder patches: s equal to 6 or 7 with k equal to 3, 4 or 5 (left shoulder opening), and s equal to 6 or 7 with k equal to 13, 14 or 15 (right shoulder opening). Emit the 9-quad manifold crown cap on station 23: for j from 0 below 9, `addq`(`VROW`[20 times 23 plus j], `VROW`[20 times 23 plus j plus 1], `VROW`[20 times 23 plus 18 minus j], `VROW`[20 times 23 plus 19 minus j], 12), shifting the inner crown vertices smoothly up to Z equal to H so the top of the skull is rounded. Emit the crotch perineum quad `addq`(`VROW`[0], `VROW`[19], `VROW`[10], `VROW`[9], 1).

Left and right legs plus feet (X-mirrored manifold 10-gon tubes from station 0 down to Z equal to 0). For side_idx 0 (left, sign 1.0, thigh bone 57, base region 23) initialize `cur`[m] as `VROW`[m] for m from 0 below 10; for side_idx 1 (right, sign negative 1.0, thigh bone 64, base region 27) initialize `cur`[m] as `VROW`[19 minus m] for m from 0 below 10 (the exact X-reflection of `VROW`[m]). Hip joint center is (sign times 0.052 times hp_k times H, 0.0, 0.472 times leg_k times H); ankle center is (sign times 0.058 times hp_k times stance_k times H, 0.008 times H, 0.048 times H); knee center is ((hip_x plus ank_x) times 0.5, negative 0.005 times H, 0.270 times leg_k times H). Record `BH` and `BT` for thigh (tb), thigh_twist (tb plus 1), calf (tb plus 2), calf_twist (tb plus 3), foot (tb plus 4), heel (tb plus 5) and ball (tb plus 6). For ring step l from 1 below 11: t is `LEG_T`[l]; rad is `LEG_R`[l] times H times (cl(`MP`[14], 0.7, 1.4) when l is at most 4 else cl(`MP`[15], 0.7, 1.4)) times (1.0 plus 0.14 times (wt minus 0.5) plus 0.10 times (mus minus 0.5)); cx_l is lrp(0.052 times hp_k times H, 0.058 times hp_k times stance_k times H, t); cz is lrp(hip_z, 0.0, t); cy is lrp(0.0, ank_y, t); for m from 0 below 10, th is 2.0 times PI times ((m as real plus 0.5) divided by 10.0), px is sign times (cx_l plus rad times math::sin(th)), py is cy minus rad times math::cos(th), pz is cz, and on foot rings l equals 9 and l equals 10 elongate negative Y forward by (0.070 when l equals 9 else 0.105) times H times math::cos(th) when math::cos(th) is positive and positive Y backward by 0.028 times H times (-math::cos(th)) otherwise, setting pz to 0.0 on l equals 10. Assign smooth 2-bone twist weights to `nxt`[m]; then for m from 0 below 10 emit `addq`(`cur`[(m plus 1) mod 10], `cur`[m], `nxt`[m], `nxt`[(m plus 1) mod 10], r_leg) when side_idx equals 0, and the X-reflected quad `addq`(`cur`[m], `cur`[(m plus 1) mod 10], `nxt`[(m plus 1) mod 10], `nxt`[m], r_leg) when side_idx equals 1; copy `nxt` into `cur`. After ring 10, close the plantar sole with the 4 manifold quads `addq`(`cur`[9 minus j], `cur`[8 minus j], `cur`[j plus 1], `cur`[j], reg_base plus 3) when side_idx equals 0 and `addq`(`cur`[j], `cur`[j plus 1], `cur`[8 minus j], `cur`[9 minus j], reg_base plus 3) when side_idx equals 1 for j from 0 below 4.

Left and right arms, wrists, palms and all 10 five-jointed fingers with exact X-reflection symmetry. For side_idx 0 (left, sign 1.0) `cur` is [`VROW`[123], `VROW`[124], `VROW`[125], `VROW`[126], `VROW`[146], `VROW`[166], `VROW`[165], `VROW`[164], `VROW`[163], `VROW`[143]], and for side_idx 1 (right, sign negative 1.0) `cur` is the exact `19 minus k` X-reflection [`VROW`[136], `VROW`[135], `VROW`[134], `VROW`[133], `VROW`[153], `VROW`[173], `VROW`[174], `VROW`[175], `VROW`[176], `VROW`[156]]. Bone indices match `BPAR_TAB`: ab is 15 on left and 36 on right, rb is 15 on left and 19 on right, thumb_b is 22 on left and 43 on right. Compute left-side reference arm geometry first: sx_l is 0.105 times sh_k times H, sy is 0.0, sz is 0.785 times H, unit axis (ax_l, ay, az) is normalized (math::cos(arm_deg times D2R), negative 0.02, negative math::sin(arm_deg times D2R)), alen is 0.370 times arm_k times H, radial horizontal basis (rx_l, ry, 0) is normalized (-ay, ax_l, 0), and dorsal basis (ux_l, uy, uz) is normalized (-az times ax_l, -az times ay, 1.0 minus az times az); then on side_idx, every X coordinate of bone heads/tails (`BH`, `BT`) and ring vertices `nxt`[m] is `sign` times the left-side X coordinate while Y and Z are identical (`px = sign * (cx_l + rx_l * c1 + ux_l * c2)`, `py = cy + ry * c1 + uy * c2`, `pz = cz + uz * c2` for ph equal to `(198.0 + 36.0 * (m as real)) * D2R`). On each step `a` from 1 below 10 and m from 0 below 10 (with m1 equal to (m plus 1) mod 10): when `a` equals 9 and m equals 9 (the radial thumb saddle on both sides), call `extrude_finger`(`cur`[m], `cur`[m1], `nxt`[m1], `nxt`[m], ...) on left (side_idx 0) and the X-reflected quad `extrude_finger`(`cur`[m1], `cur`[m], `nxt`[m], `nxt`[m1], ...) on right (side_idx 1) with length `FNG_L`[0] times arm_k times H, radius `FNG_R`[0] times H, thumb_b, rb plus 3, curl 14.0; otherwise emit `addq`(`cur`[m], `cur`[m1], `nxt`[m1], `nxt`[m], reg) on left and `addq`(`cur`[m1], `cur`[m], `nxt`[m], `nxt`[m1], reg) on right; then copy `nxt` into `cur`. Finally on the distal palm loop `cur`, for j from 0 below 4: fi is j plus 1 (1 index, 2 middle, 3 ring, 4 pinky), bb is (24 plus 3 times j) on left and (45 plus 3 times j) on right; call `extrude_finger` on (`cur`[j], `cur`[j plus 1], `cur`[8 minus j], `cur`[9 minus j]) when side_idx equals 0 and on (`cur`[9 minus j], `cur`[8 minus j], `cur`[j plus 1], `cur`[j]) when side_idx equals 1, with length `FNG_L`[fi] times arm_k times H, radius `FNG_R`[fi] times H, and curl 12.0 plus 3.0 times (fi as real).

Optional eyeball quad meshes and full skeleton/landmark population. Record head, neck, spine, pelvis, jaw (6), eye_l (7), eye_r (8), brow_l (9), brow_r (10), cheek_l (11), cheek_r (12), breast_l (13) and breast_r (14) `BH` and `BT` coordinates from the morphed head and torso geometry, and fill all 39 3D landmarks in `LM` (crown, forehead, glabella, brow_l, brow_r, eye_l, eye_r, nose_bridge, nose_tip, lips_upper, lips_lower, chin, jaw_l, jaw_r, ear_l, ear_r, neck_front, neck_back, clavicle_l, clavicle_r, shoulder_l, shoulder_r, chest, bust_l, bust_r, waist, navel, hips, crotch, elbow_l, elbow_r, wrist_l, wrist_r, hand_l, hand_r, knee_l, knee_r, ankle_l, ankle_r). When `WITH_EYES` is not 0, for eye_side 0 (left, bone 7, sign 1.0) and 1 (right, bone 8, sign negative 1.0), build a watertight all-quad eyeball centered at `BH` of that eye bone with radius 0.0072 times H times hd_k: 4 rings along Y (back pole to front cornea bulge) of 8 circumferential vertices, capped at back and front by the 3 manifold quads (0,1,6,7), (1,2,5,6) and (2,3,4,5) with region 30. Store bind matrices in `BM`, evaluate FACS blendshapes and current bone pose via `hc_update()`, run `hc_audit()`, call `refresh_views()`, and return `NV` as i32.

`hc_update()` is exported and applies all 52 ARKit FACS expression weights in `FC` plus all 71 bone Euler rotations in `BP` from `REST` into `POS`, then recomputes `NRM` and refreshes views. First copy `REST` (3 times `NV` entries) into `TPOS`. On head vertices (`VREG`[v] from 7 through 14 or equal to 30): read rest position (x, y, z) relative to head bone `BH`[5] and normalize by head height hh (crown Z minus chin Z). Apply symmetric/asymmetric FACS displacements (`FC`[0] jawOpen lowers chin/jaw/lower-lip Z and rotates backward in Y; `FC`[1], `FC`[2] mouthSmileLeft/Right pull mouth corners outward in X and upward in Z; `FC`[3], `FC`[4] mouthFrownLeft/Right pull mouth corners downward; `FC`[5] mouthPucker and `FC`[6] mouthFunnel narrow lip X and push lips forward in negative Y; `FC`[7], `FC`[8] mouthLeft/Right shift lips in X; `FC`[9], `FC`[10] mouthUpperUpLeft/Right raise upper lip; `FC`[11], `FC`[12] mouthLowerDownLeft/Right lower lower lip; `FC`[13] through `FC`[16] mouthPress/Stretch compress or widen lips; `FC`[17] browInnerUp raises glabella and inner brows; `FC`[18], `FC`[19] browDownLeft/Right lower brows and furrow glabella; `FC`[20], `FC`[21] browOuterUpLeft/Right raise outer brows; `FC`[22], `FC`[23] eyeBlinkLeft/Right close upper eyelid down to eye center; `FC`[24], `FC`[25] eyeWideLeft/Right raise upper eyelid; `FC`[26], `FC`[27] eyeSquintLeft/Right raise lower eyelid; `FC`[28] cheekPuff inflates cheeks outward; `FC`[29], `FC`[30] cheekSquintLeft/Right lift cheeks; `FC`[31], `FC`[32] noseSneerLeft/Right raise nasal alae; `FC`[33] through `FC`[35] jawForward/Left/Right shift jaw; `FC`[36] through `FC`[51] viseme/tongue/gaze channels modulate lip opening, rounding and eye rotation). Next build the 71 world bone transforms in `WM` in bone order 0 through 70: for bone b, local rotation matrix R_loc comes from Euler angles (`BP`[3 times b], `BP`[3 times b plus 1], `BP`[3 times b plus 2]) in degrees around X, Y, Z pivoted at rest head `BH`; when `BPAR`[b] is negative, world transform is (R_loc, h minus R_loc times h), otherwise compose parent world transform with local transform around parent-transformed head so child bones inherit parent motion cleanly. For each vertex v from 0 below `NV`, blend its 4 bone transforms (`JW`, `WW`) on `TPOS` and re-project radial distance from the dominant bone segment toward its rest distance by factor 0.35 when two bones blend (eliminating linear-blend candy-wrapper collapse on forearm and thigh twist), writing `POS`. Finally call `recalc_nrm`(`POS`, `TRI`, `NT`, `NRM`, `NV`) and `refresh_views()`.

`hc_audit() i32` is exported and computes 25 quantitative anatomical, topological and rig diagnostics into `AUD`, returning the count of critical findings as i32. From `REST`, `POS`, `QUAD`, `TRI`, `WW`, `LM` and `GPOS` (when `GNV` is above 0): `AUD`[0] is stature in meters (max Z minus min Z of body vertices where `VREG` is below 30); `AUD`[1] is stature in inches (`AUD`[0] divided by 0.0254); `AUD`[2] is head_heights (`AUD`[0] divided by max(crown Z minus chin Z, 1e-7)); for station X-extent helper `xext(s)`, scan `k` from 0 below 20 and skip any `VROW`[20 times s plus k] below 0 before taking max X minus min X; `AUD`[3] is bi-deltoid shoulder breadth (`xext`(8)) divided by stature; `AUD`[4] is waist_breadth (`xext`(3)) divided by stature; `AUD`[5] is hip_breadth (`xext`(1)) divided by stature; `AUD`[6] is crotch_height divided by stature; `AUD`[7] is anatomical arm_span (the sum of 3D segment lengths across `LM` landmarks shoulder_r(21) to shoulder_l(20), shoulder_l(20) to elbow_l(29), elbow_l(29) to wrist_l(31), 2.2 times wrist_l(31) to hand_l(33), shoulder_r(21) to elbow_r(30), elbow_r(30) to wrist_r(32), and 2.2 times wrist_r(32) to hand_r(34)) divided by stature; `AUD`[8] is ANSUR II RMS percent deviation across shoulder, waist, hip and crotch ratios against sex-interpolated ANSUR II medians (shoulder 0.245 female to 0.275 male, waist 0.152 to 0.168, hip 0.208 to 0.192, crotch 0.468 to 0.476); `AUD`[9] is rest-pose L/R symmetry max error in millimeters (for each body vertex on positive X, distance from (-x, y, z) to nearest negative-X body vertex times 1000.0); `AUD`[10] is unweighted vertex count (sum of 4 weights below 0.99); `AUD`[11] is garment poke-through vertex count (when `GNV` is above 0, count of garment vertices `GPOS` whose signed offset `(g minus p_near) dot n_near` against the nearest `POS` body vertex is below negative 0.0002 m) and `AUD`[12] is worst poke-through depth in millimeters; `AUD`[13] is open boundary edge count of `QUAD` (0 when watertight; check every undirected quad edge `(min, max)` has count 2) and `AUD`[14] is non-manifold edge count (count above 2); `AUD`[15] is forearm twist cross-section retention percent: across forearm vertices (`VREG`[v] equal to 16), measure mean perpendicular distance r0 from `REST`[v] to the segment `BH`[18]..`BT`[20], then blend 45-degree axial rotation around that segment for bone 20 (`forearm_twist_l`) and 90-degree axial rotation for bone 21 (`hand_l`) using each vertex's `JW`/`WW` weights plus the 0.35 radial volume-preservation blend from `hc_update`, measure the twisted mean perpendicular distance r1, and set `AUD`[15] to 100.0 times (r1 divided by max(r0, 1e-7)); `AUD`[16] is total quad count `NQ` as real; `AUD`[17] is total bone count 71.0; `AUD`[18] is active FACS count. Return the number of critical issues (`AUD`[10] above 0, `AUD`[11] above 0, `AUD`[13] above 0, `AUD`[14] above 0, or `AUD`[2] outside 5.5 to 9.5) as i32.

`hc_garment(kind i32, offset real, z_lo real, z_hi real, flare real, drape_iters i32) i32` is exported and builds an all-quad body-fitted garment shell directly from the current `POS`, `NRM`, `UV`, `QUAD`, `VREG`, `JW` and `WW` into `GPOS`, `GNRM`, `GUV`, `GQUAD`, `GTRI`, `GJW` and `GWW`, returning `GNV` as i32. Kind 0 is top/tank/shirt (keeps torso and optionally upper-arm quads where Z divided by H is between z_lo and z_hi and excludes head, hands and legs), kind 1 is shorts/pants (keeps pelvis and leg quads where Z divided by H is between z_lo and z_hi), kind 2 is skirt (builds a clean 20-around by 14-ring pleated A-line quad tube from waist Z equal to z_hi times H down to hem Z equal to z_lo times H using convex radial hull over pelvis/thigh `POS` plus `offset` plus `flare` times v, copying nearest body 4-bone weights), kind 3 is boots/socks (keeps lower-leg and foot quads below z_hi times H), kind 4 is gloves (keeps wrist, palm and finger quads), and kind 5 is scalp/hair cap (keeps cranial/crown quads above brow/ear line with hairline taper). For shell kinds (0, 1, 3, 4, 5), remap every vertex of kept quads into `GPOS`, `GUV`, `GJW`, `GWW`, displace outward along body normal by `offset` (plus `flare` near lower hem), then run `drape_iters` passes of Laplacian quad-neighbor smoothing followed after EVERY pass by an anti-poke-through clamp against its source body vertex so `(GPOS[v] minus POS[src]) dot NRM[src]` is at least `offset` times 0.85. After building ANY garment kind (0 through 5), run 2 passes of global nearest-body-vertex anti-poke-through clamping on every garment vertex `g` from 0 below `GNV`: find the closest body vertex `bi` (`VREG`[bi] below 30) in `POS`, compute signed normal clearance `sd = (GPOS[g] - POS[bi]) dot NRM[bi]`, and whenever `sd` is below `offset * 0.5` push `GPOS[g]` outward along `NRM[bi]` by `(offset * 0.5 - sd)` so zero vertices ever penetrate the skin. Recompute `GNRM` with `recalc_nrm`, update `AUD`[11] and `AUD`[12], call `refresh_views()`, and return `GNV` as i32.

`hc_alloc_deform(nv i32, nt i32)` is exported for general-purpose `mesh_edit` acceleration on arbitrary meshes: it sets `SNV` to nv and `SNT` to nt, sizes `SPOS` (3·nv), `SNRM` (3·nv), `STRI` (3·nt), `TPOS` (3·nv) and `SMASK` (nv), and calls `refresh_views()`.

`hc_shrinkwrap(offset real, relax_iters i32) i32` is exported and snaps every selected vertex (`SMASK`[v] not 0) in `TPOS` (count `SNV`) onto the surface of the target mesh (`SPOS`, `STRI`, `SNT`, or onto `POS`/`NRM` of the human when `SNT` equals 0) at normal distance `offset`, optionally running `relax_iters` tangential smoothing passes while clamping above the surface, and returns the number of moved vertices as i32.

`hc_prop_edit(mode i32, cx real, cy real, cz real, dx real, dy real, dz real, rad real, deg real, falloff i32, sym_x i32) i32` is exported and applies Blender-style proportional editing to `TPOS` (count `SNV`): for each vertex v, d is the distance from `TPOS`[v] to (cx, cy, cz) (or the smaller of distance to (cx, cy, cz) and (-cx, cy, cz) with mirrored X displacement when sym_x is not 0); when d is below rad, u is 1.0 minus d divided by rad, weight w is u·u·(3.0 minus 2.0·u) for falloff 0 (smooth), sqrt(cl(2.0·u minus u·u, 0.0, 1.0)) for falloff 1 (sphere), u·u for falloff 2 (sharp), and u for falloff 3 (linear); mode 0 translates by w·(dx, dy, dz), mode 1 scales about (cx, cy, cz) by 1.0 plus w·(dx minus 1.0, dy minus 1.0, dz minus 1.0), and mode 2 rotates about axis (dx, dy, dz) through (cx, cy, cz) by w·deg degrees. It returns the count of affected vertices as i32.

`main()` does nothing.
